---
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import GovNav from '../../components/GovNav.astro';
import { BYLAWS } from '../../data/site';
---
<Base title="Bylaws" description="The USPSA Alabama Section bylaws, current revision and history.">
  <PageHead title="Section bylaws" lede="Section bylaws are subordinate to the USPSA Bylaws and rules of competition. USPSA must be given a copy after every amendment and at every Section Coordinator election; if a Section stops filing them, USPSA's default standards apply instead (Policy §2.5-2.6)." />
  <div class="container">
    <GovNav />

    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="eyebrow">Current</span>
        <h3>{BYLAWS.current.label}</h3>
        <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={BYLAWS.current.file}>Download PDF</a></p>
        <p class="meta">Recovered from an archived copy of the previous Section website. Signed copy on file with USPSA: <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Previous revisions</h3>
        <ul>
          {BYLAWS.history.map((b) => <li><a href={b.file} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{b.label}</a></li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Summary of the 2019 bylaws</h2>
      <p>A plain-language summary. The PDF controls.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Art.</th><th>Subject</th><th>What it says</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1-2</td><td>Name, objectives</td><td>The Alabama Section covers the State of Alabama. Purpose: grow practical shooting, foster cooperation among clubs, promote the sport.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3</td><td>Membership</td><td>Clubs must be USPSA-affiliated first, sign the bylaws, be recommended by the SC, and be approved by Executive Committee vote; conflicting match dates with nearby clubs are grounds for denial. Individuals are Section members if they are USPSA members in good standing and Alabama residents.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4-5</td><td>Organization, voting</td><td>Executive Committee = Section Coordinator (chair) + each club president or designee. One vote per club. Non-voting advisors allowed.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6</td><td>Meetings</td><td>At least one meeting a year, during or right after the Section Championship. Special meetings by the SC or any two members, and may be held electronically. Quorum is a majority.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>7</td><td>Jurisdiction, election, expenses</td><td>SC has jurisdiction over USPSA rules/policy and Nationals slots; the Committee over everything else. SC term is one year (1 Apr - 31 Mar), elected one vote per club. $20 per club per year, due before 30 Jan, with an annual accounting. Travel, meals, and match fees are not allowable expenses.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>8</td><td>Representatives</td><td>Club presidents sit on the Committee or appoint a designee.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>9</td><td>Activity credits</td><td>All clubs' activity fees pool into one Section count for Nationals slot purposes.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10</td><td>Section Championship</td><td>Held annually by one host club chosen by the Committee, which acts as steering committee. Host keeps proceeds after fees and expenses. Section Champion titles for Alabama residents in each recognized division.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>11</td><td>Slot distribution</td><td>By placement at the Section Championship, division champions first. Leftover slots by random drawing. <strong>The drawing conflicts with USPSA policy §2.5(d); the Section now awards slots by <a href="/nationals-slots/">application</a> and an amendment is pending.</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>12</td><td>Signatories</td><td>Club representatives as of Feb 2019. Reviewed by the SC whenever club representation changes.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>Amending the bylaws</h2>
        <p>The 2019 bylaws do not set a notice period for amendments. In practice: the proposed text goes out with the meeting agenda, the Executive Committee votes (majority of a quorum, Art. 6.B), and the amended bylaws are sent to the Area 6 Director and the USPSA national office (Policy §2.6(a)) and posted here. Recommended: adopt a 14-day written notice requirement in the next amendment so the process is documented.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
